      "properties": {
        "reported": true,
        "property_type": "magnetic",
        "summary": "Dc susceptibility (1.8–300 K, 0.1 T) shows dominant intracluster antiferromagnetic interactions: χT = 45.8 cm3 K mol−1 at RT (expected 54.25) and 14.8 cm3 K mol−1 at 1.8 K; Curie–Weiss fit above 100 K gives C = 44.3 cm3 K mol−1 and θ = −20.5 K. Magnetization at 7 T and 1.8 K is 28.1 μB without saturation. No out-of-phase ac signal above 1.8 K. 57Fe Mössbauer spectra (3–295 K) show paramagnetic FeIII quadrupole doublets at high T and only slight broadening at 3 K, consistent with faster magnetic relaxation than in the Tb, Er, and Dy analogues.",
        "measurements": [
          {
            "property_type": "magnetic",
            "name": "χT",
            "value": 45.8,
            "unit": "cm3 K mol−1",
            "conditions": "room temperature, dc 0.1 T"
          },
          {
            "property_type": "magnetic",
            "name": "χT",
            "value": 14.8,
            "unit": "cm3 K mol−1",
